    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/nfdi4cat/goldbook-skos/blame/main/vocabularies/goldbook/IDs00xxx/00268.ttl> ;
    skos:definition "Cations formally derived by the addition of one hydron to the $\\ce{N}$ or $\\ce{O}$ atom of an amide and $N$-hydrocarbyl derivatives thereof. In organic chemistry an unspecified amidium ion is commonly a carboxamidium ion  or  The term does not imply knowledge concerning the position of the cationic centre, e.g. $\\ce{PhC(=O)N^{+}Me3}$ N,N,N-trimethylbenzamidium."@en ;
    skos:inScheme goldbook: ;
    skos:prefLabel "amidium ions"@en ;
